`LICENSE`); its own data is CC BY 4.0 (see `LICENSE-DATA`).

1. τ²-bench — external benchmark
--------------------------------
τ²-bench is an agent benchmark published by Sierra Research. It is an
independent, third-party benchmark: a user simulator converses with the agent,
which must drive domain tools against a live domain database, and scoring
checks the resulting database state plus natural-language assertions.

- Upstream repository: https://github.com/sierra-research/tau2-bench
- License: see the upstream repository — we do not restate its license name or
  terms here.

What this repository redistributes: **derived indexes only.**
`benchmarks/tau2/retail_manifest.json`, `airline_manifest.json`, and
`telecom_manifest.json` contain one row per (task id, harness) holding the
outcome of our own runs (`status`, `reward`, `wall`). They are keyed by
upstream task id. No upstream task text, task prompts, user-simulator scripts,
tool schemas, or domain databases are included, and the manifests are not a
substitute for the upstream package — to re-run the benchmark, obtain it from
the upstream repository above.

- Our numbers use a modified protocol (local model, cloud user simulator)
  rather than the official setup; see `benchmarks/README.md`. They are not
  directly comparable to upstream leaderboard numbers.

2. Other external benchmarks evaluated during development
---------------------------------------------------------
At least one further external benchmark was evaluated during development
against its own published task and answer files. Those files, and any derived
artifacts from them — including result tables, per-item scores, and score
summaries — are **not** redistributed in this repository, because the task and
answer sets are not ours to republish. Evaluation of that benchmark therefore
cannot be repeated from this repository alone; obtain it from its own upstream
source.

No third-party benchmark's task set or answer set is included anywhere in this
repository. The benchmarks whose data *is* published here (LRAB and the
mechanism, ablation, frontier-probe, safety, and failure-form studies) are
built from author-written synthetic tasks; see `LICENSE-DATA`.

3. Model weights
----------------
No model weights are distributed in this repository. `benchmarks/models.lock`
pins the exact Ollama model tags, manifest digests, and layer digests used for
the published runs so that a reader can pull byte-identical weights from the
upstream Ollama registry. Those weights remain under their own upstream
licenses and terms, which are not restated here.

4. Other dependencies
---------------------
Runtime dependencies are declared in `requirements.txt` and remain under their
own upstream licenses. No vendored third-party source is included in this
repository.
